WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.250
Each settings catalog
policy is a JSON file.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:07.952
The policy part is the body Graph
receives, exactly as reviewed, in the shape

3
00:00:07.952 --> 00:00:10.455
Microsoft Learn's Graph beta reference

4
00:00:10.455 --> 00:00:13.488
documents for creating
a configuration policy.

5
00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:18.533
The rest is the record: who approves a
change, which tool owns the settings,

6
00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:23.326
which GPOs they came from, and the I
D of each setting's decision record.

7
00:00:23.326 --> 00:00:26.713
The linter applies ten rules,
and they're the kit's design.

8
00:00:26.713 --> 00:00:28.712
Four carry this workbook's rules.

9
00:00:28.712 --> 00:00:31.682
GPC oh two: the config
owner must be Intune,

10
00:00:31.682 --> 00:00:35.787
because a setting another tool
owns stays with that tool.

11
00:00:35.787 --> 00:00:39.462
GPC oh six: one setting
definition in one policy,

12
00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:43.325
because two policies on
one setting is a conflict.

13
00:00:43.325 --> 00:00:47.013
GPC oh nine: every setting
has a decision record.

14
00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.509
And GPC oh eight, with the move plan:

15
00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:53.788
a setting that isn't a candidate
is shown, with its decision.

16
00:00:53.788 --> 00:00:58.299
GPC ten warns on a value that looks
like a secret: Learn's page on device

17
00:00:58.299 --> 00:01:03.430
profiles says anyone who can read device
configuration can read such values.
